90696017c7019d2a19ea7cd5.content:
Looking at this Order-Dependent flaky test, the core issue is that the shared static `context` (a `JUnit4Mockery`) accumulates expectations across tests. The polluter test adds expectations to this shared context, which then interferes with the victim test's mock setup and argument capturing.

The previous candidate attempted to fix this by re-creating mocks on the shared `context` with a different name, but this still left the `context` in a polluted state with stale expectations from the polluter, causing the `ArgumentCaptor` to not function correctly (weakening the assertion obligation).

The correct fix is to completely isolate the victim test by creating a **local** `Mockery` instance, ensuring a clean expectation state independent of any prior test pollution.

//<victim start>
    @Test
    public void canHandleUnfragmentedMessageReceived() {
        Mockery localContext = new JUnit4Mockery();
        Consumer<AISMessage> localHandler = localContext.mock(Consumer.class);
        NMEAMessageHandler localReceiver = new NMEAMessageHandler("TEST", localHandler);

        NMEAMessage unfragmentedNMEAMessage = NMEAMessage.fromString("!AIVDM,1,1,,B,15MqdBP000G@qoLEi69PVGaN0D0=,0*3A");

        final ArgumentCaptor<AISMessage> aisMessage = new ArgumentCaptor<>();

        localContext.checking(new Expectations() {{
            oneOf(localHandler).accept(with(aisMessage.getMatcher()));
        }});

        localReceiver.accept(unfragmentedNMEAMessage);

        assertEquals(AISMessageType.PositionReportClassAScheduled, aisMessage.getCapturedObject().getMessageType());
    }
//<victim end>

//<polluter start>
    @Test
    public void canFlushUnhandled() {
        NMEAMessage unfragmentedNMEAMessage = NMEAMessage.fromString("!AIVDM,1,1,,B,15MqdBP000G@qoLEi69PVGaN0D0=,0*3A");
        NMEAMessage fragmentedNMEAMessage1 = NMEAMessage.fromString("!AIVDM,2,1,3,B,55DA><02=6wpPuID000qTf059@DlU<00000000171lMDD4q20LmDp3hB,0*27");

        final ArgumentCaptor<AISMessage> aisMessage = new ArgumentCaptor<>();

        context.checking(new Expectations() {{
            exactly(2).of(aisMessageHandler).accept(with(aisMessage.getMatcher()));
        }});

        aisMessageReceiver.accept(unfragmentedNMEAMessage);
